# Google Drive backup for builds made from source.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (next to package.json) and fill in the OAuth client of a Google Cloud project you own,
# created as type "Desktop app". See docs/GOOGLE_DRIVE_SETUP.md for every step.
#
# The values are built into the app when it is compiled (src-tauri/build.rs reads this file). Official releases get
# them from the GitHub Actions secrets of the same names instead. `.env` is ignored by git: never commit it.
#
# Leave both empty to build ChatVault without Google Drive; everything else works the same.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# Google treats a desktop app's client secret as public (anyone can read it from the program), but its token endpoint
# still expects it for "Desktop app" clients, so it is sent along. It is not relied on for security: PKCE is.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
